# gvisor.env — the ONE place the gVisor release is pinned (setec#89).
#
# Three consumers read this file and carry no version of their own:
#   Dockerfile.installer                        build args from .github/workflows/images.yml
#   development/k3s/scripts/*                   source it when preparing a node by hand
#   .github/workflows/e2e.yml                   no longer preps gvisor itself; the
#                                               installer image does, from this pin
# scripts/check-runtime-pins.sh fails CI when any of them re-adds a literal.
#
# The installer lays gVisor on every node because nothing else does: kata-deploy
# does not ship it, and the sanctioned kind profile runs gvisor as its ONE
# backend. Before this pin existed, a plain `helm install` produced a node
# advertising runtime.gvisor=false and no Sandbox ever scheduled.
#
# THE WHOLE TARBALL IS SHIPPED, NOT A PRUNE. Measured on release-20260928.0: with
# only runsc and containerd-shim-runsc-v1 on disk, runsc dies at sandbox creation
# with `sidecar "gvisor_sentry" not usable ... --sidecar-usage-policy is set to
# STRICT`. The sentry is a separate binary under gvisor-bin/ now. The only policy
# that works without it is LEGACY_DEPRECATED_SLOW_EMBEDDED_FALLBACK, which
# upstream has named deprecated AND slow — on the cold-start path this repo
# exports as setec_sandbox_cold_start_seconds, for the one backend chosen
# because it has lower overhead than a microVM. Owner decision 2026-10-02: ship
# the full payload. Installer image 95 MB -> ~258 MB compressed.
#
# To bump: change both lines. GVISOR_SHA256 is the sha256 of
# gvisor-x86_64.tar.zstd from that release's SHA256SUMS. Upstream publishes no
# loose runsc binary; the URL the gVisor docs still name returns 404.
# zeroroot-ai/.github version-links.yaml watches google/gvisor releases.
GVISOR_VERSION=release-20260928.0
GVISOR_SHA256=1f2a732d12072eda6b8a64eccf9829fe9f4a1893d3292a7e8005a82089811d8d
